    "semantics": [
      "Original owners and counters are moved once with actual GunOwner private-container/role/camp/life/version/source proof. Identical string id is not ownership and onDeath retains version+1, not revive permission.",
      "All twenty original declarations remain raw byte identical inside their owning declaration (sixteen lifecycle, two player data/projection, two actual copy/gateway policies). Old player declarations retain every field/result guard and accepted shape.",
      "Grant still bind→install→counter→emit; arm resource field→owner field→emit; transfer uses same projectDeathGun→new source→delete status→bind/install new target→delete old→retired id→source event→target event. Failure preserves original prefix, not copy/rollback.",
      "First-death captures same gun and event display fields before hooks; finish later does remaining→disabled→deathExpired→emit. consumeDeathGunShot is original single write and caller retains all target/current permission checks.",
      "Entry reexports original named functions, not fresh wrappers. Lifecycle projection import points at actual player_state declaration, not entry; player state has no owner/entry import. New eager module work is only original maps, not World/query/clock/RNG/resource action.",
      "Three new literal units use actual Good-role and factory life inputs to grant/arm/transfer, failing event push at original transferred_out boundary; they compare hand event order and exact ref/stock prefix. They do not claim complete death-wave integration or use a production rule as expected-value oracle."
    ],
